      "title": "The Cloud",
      "body": "A cloud is made of water drops floating in the sky. The sky can be full of water. But most of the time you can't see the water. The drops of water form many kinds of clouds.\n\nClouds get their names in many ways. One way is by where they are found in the sky. Some clouds are high up in the sky. Some clouds are found between low and high clouds.\n\nMost of the water in clouds is in very small droplets. The droplets are so light that they float in the air. The droplets can join with other droplets to form larger drops. When that happens, gravity causes them to fall to Earth. We call the falling water drops 'rain.'",
      "source_pages": "25"
    },
    {
      "title": "Family Tree",
      "body": "A family tree is a way of showing how people in a family are related to each other. A family tree can have many branches, but a small family tree can have only one branch. A small family tree can show the father, the mother, and the siblings in a family.\n\nThe father and the mother are the parents of the siblings. The siblings are the children of the parents. The siblings can be brothers, sisters, or both. The father and the mother are married to each other. The siblings share the same parents.\n\nIn this family tree, we can see that Ali and Fatima are the father and the mother of Omar, Aisha, and Ahmed. Omar, Aisha, and Ahmed have some friends who they like, and they go out together.\n\nEL097 / QUIZ 02\n\nOmar’s best friend is Khalid, whom he met at school. They both like to play soccer and watch movies. Aisha’s best friend is Sara, whom she met at the library. They both like to read books and paint pictures. Ahmed’s best friend is Zain, whom he met at the park. They both like to ride bikes and play video games.\n\nSometimes, the siblings and their friends go out together as a group. They like to go to the mall, the cinema, or the beach. They have fun and enjoy each other’s company. They also help each other with their homework and problems. They are loyal and supportive of each other. They are not only friends but also like family.",
      "source_pages": "28-29"
    },
